1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,972
Almost four kilometers under Antarctica's ice,

2
00:00:02,972 --> 00:00:05,795
there's a lake about the size of Lake Ontario.

3
00:00:06,283 --> 00:00:07,342
It's Lake Vostok,

4
00:00:07,342 --> 00:00:12,822
one of six hundred and seventy-five lakes scientists have found hidden under Antarctica.

5
00:00:13,317 --> 00:00:16,064
Heat from inside the Earth keeps them liquid,

6
00:00:16,064 --> 00:00:20,215
even though the air above Vostok once hit minus eighty-nine degrees.

7
00:00:20,717 --> 00:00:21,202
In 2012,

8
00:00:21,202 --> 00:00:27,576
Russian scientists drilled three thousand seven hundred and sixty-nine meters down and reached the water.

9
00:00:28,083 --> 00:00:30,557
Hit like and subscribe for more hidden worlds.

10
00:00:30,857 --> 00:00:34,587
The lake may have been sealed off for at least fourteen million years.

11
00:00:34,587 --> 00:00:36,185
So, could anything live there?

12
00:00:36,683 --> 00:00:38,531
In another buried lake, Whillans,

13
00:00:38,531 --> 00:00:42,842
scientists found about a hundred and thirty thousand microbes per milliliter,

14
00:00:42,842 --> 00:00:44,186
living without sunlight.

15
00:00:44,683 --> 00:00:49,814
Vostok's ice has hinted at life too, but some scientists suspect contamination.

16
00:00:49,814 --> 00:00:51,178
The jury's still out.

17
00:00:51,683 --> 00:00:53,396
And what if all that ice melted?

18
00:00:53,396 --> 00:00:54,787
Full story on the channel.
